       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and they don't add much benefit.\n\nFor an adult with normal kidney and liver function, typical dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily. Use 2.5 mg if the patient is frail or small, or has hepatic impairment.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n\nPlease check whether 30 mg was a typo or a mix-up with another drug or formulation. If you meant 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, tell me which and I'll enter it right away. If 30 mg is truly intended, for example as part of a plan I don't have, please confirm that with your supervising resident, attending, or pharmacist first."
