     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety concern, because it's the same dose I flagged. I asked for a check with your supervising resident, attending, or pharmacist, and I can't tell whether that happened. A dose of 30 mg is three times the maximum, and I don't know of a clinical scenario where it's appropriate. I don't want to put a likely harmful order into the system on a medical student's entry alone.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily now.** This is the maximum standard dose, and your team can adjust it later.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the usual starting dose, and you can titrate up.\n- **Enter 30 mg after your attending or a pharmacist confirms it.** Give me their name and their rationale, and I'll add both to the order note. They may also prefer to enter it themselves.\n\nWhich would you like? If the aim is stronger blood pressure control, your team may prefer to add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, rather than push amlodipine past 10 mg."
      }
     ],
